uxTaskGetSystemState calls a visitor rather than filling an array.

0x73580 takes a function, a context for it and the run-time pointer, and its one
caller at 0x5c96c passes the function at the pool word 0x5c974 and a stack context. prvListTasks-
WithinSingleList at 0x9e49a fills one TaskStatus_t on its own stack per task,
hands it to the visitor and stops the walk on the first result other than pdTRUE.
There is no check against an array size, because there is no array. The walk
returns what xTaskResumeAll returns, as a tail call.

